{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please","id":1035429,"title":"Ghost Shield help please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-20T13:49:16-08:00","id":1035429,"title":"Ghost Shield help please","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw page 129</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Shield (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Streetwise, Subterfuge, Survival The caster creates a shield that protects her subject from ghostly Numina, Influences, Manifestations, Death spells, and any death-related powers of other supernatural creatures. Any power attempting to pierce the shield provokes a Clash of Wills roll.<br /> +1 Reach: The protection afforded by this spell extends to ghosts\u2019 physical attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could someone please explain to me why this has Potency as the Primary Spell Factor. I see nothing in there that would be determined by potency. Even the Clash of Will only takes into consideration Advanced Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:07:10-08:00","id":1035440,"title":"","content":"Technically a shielding spell only protects you from potency supernatural attacks. But I think this is just a typo tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:13:03-08:00","id":1035444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035440#post1035440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically a shielding spell only protects you from potency supernatural attacks. But I think this is just a typo tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect about Potency, probably correct about it being a typo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:31:15-08:00","id":1035450,"title":"","content":"I hope so because it makes no sense otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:32:03-08:00","id":1035452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035444#post1035444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect about Potency, probably correct about it being a typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>p126-127 under creative thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">These spells usually provide blanket immunity to natural or<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">mundane phenomena, while protecting against a number of</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">supernatural attacks equal to the spell\u2019s Potency. Such attacks<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">must win a Clash of Wills to affect the target.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:45:36-08:00","id":1035462,"title":"","content":"Ok but a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">directly comparable one for spirit (Ephemeral Shield, p 181) has Duration as primary.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:48:25-08:00","id":1035467,"title":"","content":"<i>I totally forgot about that creative thaumaturgy ruling. This changes quite a bit...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:48:27-08:00","id":1035468,"title":"","content":"And it should. Duration is more important because a) you usually want to have duration on a shielding spell and b) it boosts the dicepool for clashes of wills (thus making the shield better at it's job). That's why it's probably an error here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:57:59-08:00","id":1035496,"title":"","content":"But, but, but none of the blanket shielding spell's mention that they work only x times...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:32:12-08:00","id":1035511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035468#post1035468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it should. Duration is more important because a) you usually want to have duration on a shielding spell and b) it boosts the dicepool for clashes of wills (thus making the shield better at it's job). That's why it's probably an error here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they've put in a lot of primary factors that seem unnatural on purpose to encourage you to use Reach more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-20-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T01:48:33-08:00","id":1035660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035511#post1035511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they've put in a lot of primary factors that seem unnatural on purpose to encourage you to use Reach more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really doesn't make any sense. Why is it important that the Death spell should have potency while the Spirit equivalent uses duration. It's been clearly stated that the primary factor should be what makes the spell most powerful in most situations. For a shielding spell like this, it would definitly be Duration rather than potency, for reasons I allready named. I doubt they just decided to coax out more Reach and thus paradox out of players this way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:46:33-08:00","id":1035688,"title":"","content":"It seems more likely to me that, if anything, the fact that not a <b>single</b> shielding spell follows the Potency guideline re: Supernatural attacks indicates that that guideline is in error, not that all of the spells are wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035660#post1035660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That really doesn't make any sense. Why is it important that the Death spell should have potency while the Spirit equivalent uses duration. It's been clearly stated that the primary factor should be what makes the spell most powerful in most situations. For a shielding spell like this, it would definitly be Duration rather than potency, for reasons I allready named. I doubt they just decided to coax out more Reach and thus paradox out of players this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different Arcana were written by different writers, and this isn't the first example of two of them handling similar spells differently.<br /> <br /> If the Potency guideline is to be followed, they should all have Potency as their Primary.<br /> If it isn't to be followed, they should all be Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:54:15-08:00","id":1035690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035688#post1035688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems more likely to me that, if anything, the fact that not a <b>single</b> shielding spell follows the Potency guideline re: Supernatural attacks indicates that that guideline is in error, not that all of the spells are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say this looks more like the case. Way back in 2015 people started a thread collecting spells that were previewed before the book came out. Ward was one of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Ward (Space \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Subterfuge, Weaponry<br /> Space is mutable, until a magician wills otherwise. This spell locks an area down, preventing the space within from being manipulated. The Ward protects against one attempt to cast a Space spell (or similar non-Supernal magic) on a subject within the warded area per point of Potency, provoking a Clash of Wills. The mage is aware when one of her wards is attacked.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> An attempted spell only counts against the Ward\u2019s Potency if its caster wins the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\"> [2e] Spell spoiler compilation - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> You know what would be useful? A place where all the spoilered spells go together and don't have to be digged for in blog and forum posts. Death Quicken Ghost </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Comparing it to the current spell makes it seem as though they no longer intended the potency limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:57:02-08:00","id":1035691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035690#post1035690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to say this looks more like the case. Way back in 2015 people started a thread collecting spells that were previewed before the book came out. Ward was one of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Ward (Space \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Subterfuge, Weaponry<br /> Space is mutable, until a magician wills otherwise. This spell locks an area down, preventing the space within from being manipulated. The Ward protects against one attempt to cast a Space spell (or similar non-Supernal magic) on a subject within the warded area per point of Potency, provoking a Clash of Wills. The mage is aware when one of her wards is attacked.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> An attempted spell only counts against the Ward\u2019s Potency if its caster wins the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\"> [2e] Spell spoiler compilation - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> You know what would be useful? A place where all the spoilered spells go together and don't have to be digged for in blog and forum posts. Death Quicken Ghost </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Comparing it to the current spell makes it seem as though they no longer intended the potency limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent find, and makes a lot of sense. This looks like it was explicitly cut from the published spells but left in the Cr. Thaum rules by mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:25:28-08:00","id":1040276,"title":"","content":"I wish we could get a ruling on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:29:29-08:00","id":1040505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035429-ghost-shield-help-please?p=1035691#post1035691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an excellent find, and makes a lot of sense. This looks like it was explicitly cut from the published spells but left in the Cr. Thaum rules by mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. They probably realized, that a ward or shielding spell doesn't make much sense if you can just attack it with a couple of potency 1 spells and it goes down. You could not ward any kind of mystery over the centuries with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}